From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fingerprint Lab <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] goodix550c: report reply framing for the post-action failure

The first verification of a session succeeds and every later one reads a dead
sensor: an all-zero reference frame and an ADC-railed capture. Those failing
captures report an identical pixel histogram (mean 4012.1, 95.2% clipped)
across four attempts, two runs and two fingers, but four different checksums.
The same values in a different arrangement point at reads shifted by a whole
transaction rather than at a sensor that stopped working, and a reinitialize
after deactivation was measured and did not help.

Report the pack flag and byte counts of every assembled reply so a queued
reply nobody consumed becomes visible directly: it appears as a pack whose
flag or length does not match what the current command asked for.

Only framing metadata is reported. No payload is logged, and an image reply
is still encrypted at this point. The diagnostic runs under the existing
experimental gate, which is default-off at both compile time and run time.

---

--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-transport.c
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-transport.c
@@ -440,6 +440,31 @@
 
   if (goodix_proto_rx_complete (&self->rx))
     {
+      /* Reply-framing diagnostic for the post-action capture failure, where
+       * the second verification of a session reads an all-zero reference frame
+       * and an ADC-railed image whose pixel histogram repeats exactly while its
+       * arrangement does not. That shape suggests reads shifted by a whole
+       * transaction rather than a sensor fault, which this makes visible: a
+       * queued reply nobody consumed shows up here as a pack whose flag or
+       * length does not match what the current command asked for.
+       *
+       * Only the pack flag and byte counts are reported. The payload is not
+       * logged, and for an image reply it is still encrypted at this point. */
+      if (self->variant == GOODIX_VARIANT_TLS_PSK &&
+          goodix_550c_manual_fdt_poll_allowed ())
+        {
+          guint8 pack_flag = 0;
+          const guint8 *pack_payload = NULL;
+          gsize pack_payload_len = 0;
+
+          if (goodix_proto_rx_pack (&self->rx, &pack_flag, &pack_payload,
+                                    &pack_payload_len))
+            fp_dbg ("Reply framing: pack flag=0x%02x payload=%zu assembled=%zu",
+                    pack_flag, pack_payload_len, self->rx.len);
+          else
+            fp_dbg ("Reply framing: unpacked assembled=%zu", self->rx.len);
+        }
+
       /* Message complete — advance SSM */
       fpi_ssm_next_state (transfer->ssm);
     }

